<title>KENYA: Kenya coffee prices ease at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Kenya coffee prices ease at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenyan coffee prices eased on average at the weekly coffee auction on Tuesday, auction officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;Almost all grades were down following poor quality on sale,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Grade AAs averaged $389 per 50 kg, after $395 last week, while grade Ts averaged $114 against $116. Grade ABs averaged $351 from $355 previously.</p>
<p>The Coffee Board of Kenya sold 20,896 60-kg bags of coffee, compared with 24,814 last week.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom +254-2 330-261</p>
